      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SMOKEY SAINT (1) has a moderate winning strike-rate but performed well last time at Port Macquarie when second over 1512m when he did his best work late. Looks well placed and expect a big run this time. ENZONI (6) did little and finished ninth over 1512m at Port Macquarie last start, a less impressive effort than his sixth at Taree the run before. Best figures measure up nicely. Sure to run well. NARUKAMI (2) was too good for a maiden field last start over 1512m at Port Macquarie, scoring by 1.5 lengths. Liberty Smyth was in the saddle on that occasion and retains the ride. Tougher assignment this time but is one of the main contenders. TICKLE MY TOSEN (5) was out of the money when resuming from a spell last start over 1210m at Port Macquarie. Fitter now and anticipating a better run this time.",
